WEBVTT

00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:16,460
to oncologists not recognize any benefits of other care. I wouldn't necessarily agree

00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:21,020
with that. I think there are a lot of oncologists that do recognize the benefits of other care,

00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:26,940
but from a medical legal standpoint, their hands are tied. Unless they have their own private

00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:34,140
practice, they have to follow the guidelines of the practice that they belong to or the health

00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:42,380
care system that they belong to, or they will be in trouble. So they can't recommend supplements,

00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:48,380
they can't recommend hypermectin, they can't recommend rife machines, they can't recommend

00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:55,420
fennbenazone, they would get into trouble. So there they are products of the system that they

00:00:55,420 --> 00:01:05,180
belong to, and in order to not live with that mental disconnect, they have to basically buy

00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:13,020
into what they're doing. Or they, you know, it's just not healthy mentally for them. So that's what

00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:21,260
happens. So I do think there's a lot of good oncologists out there that want what's best for their

00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:33,500
patients. And if you don't feel like you have one, I'd suggest maybe look for somebody else.

